//! Code generated by superschematic topcoat. DO NOT EDIT.
//!
//! The forms of {{ .SchemaName }}: one per input type an in-process call
//! takes, and one per call with arguments a form submits. A form's struct
//! holds each field as the browser sends it, so a form that is refused
//! re-renders as it was sent; `parse` reads it by the API's rules, an input
//! type's (D14) or a route's (`Args::check`, D43); and its component
//! renders the controls with the attributes those rules give them. A
//! browser checks those attributes before it sends the form, and `parse`
//! checks every rule again.
//!
//! A control is named by its field's path: `email`, a nested object's field
//! `guest.name`, a row's `rooms[0].adults`, a list of values' `tags[0]`,
//! and an argument by its name, beside its input's fields. A form decodes
//! from the pairs a browser sends (`Form<T>`, or `from_pairs`) into its
//! struct, rows in the order of their indexes, and its errors are keyed by
//! the same names, so each message renders at its control. A list's rows
//! are added and removed by submit buttons named `_action` (`add:rooms`,
//! `remove:rooms[1]`), which `apply_action` applies without JavaScript.

